      "description": "Rows split by where the nominal class BW sits relative to GT BW, and so by which way the geometric correction has to scale: class_ok is within 10% of GT BW, upscale is at least 10% below it (the correction pushes SF up), downscale at least 10% above it (the correction pushes SF down). Columns split by the bounding-box BW measurement: measured_ok is within half an SF step of GT BW, measured_off at least half a step away. This crossing asks which way the detector misses, not which decision to fix.",
